Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => { /* app losing focus */ })
        .OnStop(activity => { /* app fully backgrounded */ }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => { /* app backgrounded */ }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- Android `OnPause` = lost focus (maps to `Deactivated`); `OnStop` = not visible (maps to `Stopped`).
- iOS `DidEnterBackground` maps to the `Stopped` window event.
- Keep handlers fast (<2 sec) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS.

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need the native callback parameters, subscribe to the `Window.Stopped` event instead — it fires on both platforms when the app backgrounds:

```csharp
// In App.cs
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* runs on all platforms */ };
    return window;
}
```
